 "experiments": [
  {
   "id": "merge",
   "title": "Two words reach one relay on the same tick",
   "what": "X sends 1 and Y sends 2 at the same moment into a relay M that listens on two faces. The standard grid ORs what arrives in the same tick into one word. FlexGrid mirrors the flex merge core, whose mode you choose.",
   "note": "arbitrate is for ALTERNATIVE paths (take one, then the other); join-or is for HALVES of one item (wait for all, then OR). The standard grid has only the second behaviour, and without waiting.",
