  {
   "id": "addsame",
   "title": "Adder, both operands on the same tick",
   "what": "A sends 7 and B sends 5 so that both reach the adder in one tick. The real flex cell takes one operand, then the other.",
   "note": "In the standard grid the two arrivals are ORed into one operand (7 OR 5 = 7) and the adder waits for a second that never comes: nothing leaves. That is the 'same-tick operand loss' on the DSL page. FlexGrid takes the lower face first, then the other, so it adds.",
